v/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000095017025103002/0000950170-25-103002-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-06-09","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02","5.07","7.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Shareholder vote results","kind":"governance","tone":"blue"},{"label":"Regulation FD disclosure","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000095017025083747/0000950170-25-083747-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-05-01","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000095017025061812/0000950170-25-061812-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["Zeta Global Holdings Corp. files with the SEC under \"Services-Prepackaged Software\", based in NY, and has been publicly reporting for 4 years.","It reported $1.3bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 49.9% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 59.0%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($129.3m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 49.9% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $396.3m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"},{"text":"Gross margin of 59.0% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001851003"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $129.3m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"},{"text":"Net cash of $91.5m against total assets of $1.4bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"}],"bear":[{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 60.9% to 59.0% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001851003"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-4.8% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $2.7m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 12.2% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526199156/0001193125-26-199156-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-199156"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.7% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1851003/000119312526294919/0001193125-26-294919-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 51.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.51,"consecutive":2,"current":0.59,"current_display":"59.0%","threshold_display":"51.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 25.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.25,"consecutive":2,"current":0.499,"current_display":"49.9%","threshold_display":"25.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 19.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.19,"consecutive":1,"current":0.122,"current_display":"12.2%","threshold_display":"19.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.224,"current_display":"0.22","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","